# Pairs with ReadPositionHonest, and reproduces issue #4634 as production had it:
# the leaf keeps no durable record that it has held snapshot coverage, so once
# the snapshot vanishes its cold start sees "no snapshot", replays the surviving
# WAL suffix and serves a read position past an owned write the GC trimmed under
# the snapshot. The mutation enables snapshot loss and the two faults it needs.
# The base raises the record in the leaf row before any pin that relies on it.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestSnapshotRecordNeverRaised
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: no record of held snapshot coverage, so a cold start over a vanished snapshot replays a trimmed WAL
PERTURBS: PublishPin

--- FIND
                  THEN [hadSnap EXCEPT ![l] = @ \/ cov[l] # NoSnap]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the record is never raised.
                  THEN hadSnap
--- END
--- FIND
SnapshotLoss == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the environment may destroy a snapshot.
SnapshotLoss == TRUE
--- END

--- FIND
MaxFaults == 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the snapshot vanishes and its leaf stops: two faults.
MaxFaults == 2
--- END